# [SONNET-4.6] sq-zgbso.2 — ODRL stateless core: stratum C.
# Input: the serialized closure of stratum B (includes A + B derived facts).
#
# NAF in this stratum is over stratum B's COMPLETE andSubUnsat and prohibMatches:
#   - odrlx:lcSat for odrl:and  — derived if no sub-constraint is andSubUnsat
#   - auth:* grant triples      — emitted when no prohibition matches the request
#
# Three grant rules cover all permission shapes in scope:
#   1. Unconstrained permission (no odrl:constraint)
#   2. Permission with ONLY atomic constraints (checked via anyPermConstrUnsat from B)
#   3. Permission with a satisfied logical constraint (lcSat from A or C)

@prefix odrl:  <http://www.w3.org/ns/odrl/2/> .
@prefix auth:  <https://sparq.dev/ns/auth#> .
@prefix odrlx: <https://sparq.dev/ns/odrlx#> .
@prefix log:   <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/log#> .

# ── odrl:and logical constraint satisfied ────────────────────────────────────
# Derived when NO sub-constraint is in andSubUnsat (all must be in atomicSat from A).
# Requires at least one sub-constraint (the odrl:and ?c pattern guards this).
# NAF is over stratum B's andSubUnsat, which is complete before this stratum.
{ ?lc odrl:and ?c .
  ?req a odrl:Request .
  ?S log:notIncludes { ?lc odrlx:andSubUnsat ?req } . }
=> { ?lc odrlx:lcSat ?req } .

# ── grant rule 1: UNCONSTRAINED permission ────────────────────────────────────
# Fires when the permission has no odrl:constraint at all. NAF is over:
#   - INPUT  predicate odrl:constraint (input-complete, safe in any stratum)
#   - stratum B predicate prohibMatches (complete before this stratum)
{ ?pol odrl:permission ?perm .
  ?perm odrl:action ?act ; odrl:target ?tgt ; odrl:assignee ?party .
  ?act odrlx:mode ?mode .
  ?req a odrl:Request ; odrl:action ?act ; odrl:target ?tgt ; odrl:assignee ?party .
  ?S1 log:notIncludes { ?perm odrl:constraint ?anyc } .
  ?S2 log:notIncludes { ?proh odrlx:prohibMatches ?req } . }
=> { ?party ?mode ?tgt } .

# ── grant rule 2: permission with ONLY atomic constraints (all satisfied) ─────
# Fires when the permission has at least one atomic constraint (?c odrl:leftOperand ?lo)
# and no logical constraint (S2-S4 check odrl:or/and/xone). NAF is over:
#   - stratum B's anyPermConstrUnsat (all atomic constraints satisfied)
#   - INPUT  predicates odrl:or/and/xone (no LC present)
#   - stratum B's prohibMatches (no prohibition matches)
{ ?pol odrl:permission ?perm .
  ?perm odrl:action ?act ; odrl:target ?tgt ; odrl:assignee ?party .
  ?perm odrl:constraint ?c . ?c odrl:leftOperand ?lo .
  ?act odrlx:mode ?mode .
  ?req a odrl:Request ; odrl:action ?act ; odrl:target ?tgt ; odrl:assignee ?party .
  ?S1 log:notIncludes { ?perm odrlx:anyPermConstrUnsat ?req } .
  ?S2 log:notIncludes { ?perm odrl:constraint ?lc . ?lc odrl:or ?x } .
  ?S3 log:notIncludes { ?perm odrl:constraint ?lc . ?lc odrl:and ?x } .
  ?S4 log:notIncludes { ?perm odrl:constraint ?lc . ?lc odrl:xone ?x } .
  ?S5 log:notIncludes { ?proh odrlx:prohibMatches ?req } . }
=> { ?party ?mode ?tgt } .

# ── grant rule 3: permission with a satisfied logical constraint ───────────────
# Fires when the permission has a logical constraint ?lc that is satisfied (lcSat from
# stratum A for odrl:or, or from this stratum for odrl:and). Uses lcSat POSITIVELY —
# no NAF on the derived lcSat fact, so no cycle within stratum C. NAF is over:
#   - stratum B's anyPermConstrUnsat (all atomic constraints on the permission satisfied)
#   - stratum B's prohibMatches (no prohibition matches)
{ ?pol odrl:permission ?perm .
  ?perm odrl:action ?act ; odrl:target ?tgt ; odrl:assignee ?party .
  ?perm odrl:constraint ?lc .
  ?lc odrlx:lcSat ?req .
  ?act odrlx:mode ?mode .
  ?req a odrl:Request ; odrl:action ?act ; odrl:target ?tgt ; odrl:assignee ?party .
  ?S1 log:notIncludes { ?perm odrlx:anyPermConstrUnsat ?req } .
  ?S2 log:notIncludes { ?proh odrlx:prohibMatches ?req } . }
=> { ?party ?mode ?tgt } .
